---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { profile } from '../../data/profile';
import { englishProjects } from '../../data/english';

const featured = englishProjects.filter((project) => ['01', '06', '07', '08'].includes(project.number));
const systems = englishProjects.filter((project) => ['02', '03', '04', '05', '09', '10'].includes(project.number));
---
<Base lang="en" title={`${profile.name} — Multiplatform Software Engineer`} description="Miguel's portfolio: Flutter, Rust, local systems, Next.js and Astro.">
  <main id="contenido">
    <section class="hero wrap">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <div class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span> Open to opportunities</div>
        <p class="hero-index">PORTFOLIO / 2026</p>
        <h1>From product idea.<br /><em>To working software.</em></h1>
        <p class="hero-lede">I build multiplatform software with Flutter and Rust, from the interface to synchronization between devices. I also develop web products with Next.js and Astro.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href="#proyectos">Explore projects ↘</a><a class="button button-outline" href={profile.github} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub ↗</a></div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-visual" aria-label="Diagram showing product, interface, systems and platform layers">
        <div class="visual-top"><span>HOW I WORK</span><span>01 / 04</span></div>
        <div class="visual-orbit orbit-one"></div><div class="visual-orbit orbit-two"></div>
        <div class="visual-center"><span>FROM IDEA</span><strong>TO SOFTWARE</strong><span>THAT WORKS</span></div>
        <div class="visual-node node-a">01 <strong>PRODUCT</strong></div><div class="visual-node node-b">02 <strong>INTERFACE</strong></div><div class="visual-node node-c">03 <strong>SYSTEMS</strong></div><div class="visual-node node-d">04 <strong>PLATFORM</strong></div>
        <div class="visual-bottom"><span>Flutter · Rust · Web · Native</span><span>↗</span></div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <div class="ticker" aria-label="Areas of work"><div>PRODUCT <span>✳</span> MULTIPLATFORM <span>✳</span> LOCAL NETWORKS <span>✳</span> SYSTEMS <span>✳</span> USER EXPERIENCE <span>✳</span> NATIVE INTEGRATION</div></div>
    <section class="proof-strip wrap" aria-label="Selected strengths">
      <div><span>01 / SYSTEMS</span><strong>Local P2P network</strong><p>Device communication with deferred remote synchronization.</p></div>
      <div><span>02 / PRODUCT</span><strong>Flutter + Rust</strong><p>Multiplatform interfaces connected to native logic.</p></div>
      <div><span>03 / EXPERIENCE</span><strong>Interactive editor</strong><p>2D and isometric floor planning interfaces.</p></div>
    </section>
    <section class="section wrap" id="proyectos">
      <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="section-kicker">01 / WORK</p><h2>Products with<br /><em>real context.</em></h2></div><p>Four independent projects. Meson is the largest; its key systems have separate technical cases.</p></div>
      <div class="project-grid">{featured.map((project) => <a class={`project-card accent-${project.accent}`} href={`/en/projects/${project.slug}/`}><div class="project-top"><span>{project.number} / PROJECT</span><span class="card-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div><div class="project-art" aria-hidden="true"><span class="art-frame"><span class="art-grid"></span><span class="art-symbol">{project.number === '01' ? 'M' : project.number === '06' ? 'N' : '◇'}</span></span></div><div class="project-copy"><p class="project-type">{project.type}</p><h3>{project.title}</h3><p>{project.description}</p><div class="tags">{project.stack.map((skill) => <span>{skill}</span>)}</div></div></a>)}</div>
      <div class="subsection-heading"><p class="section-kicker">INSIDE MESON</p><h3>Architecture and interfaces.</h3><p>Technical cases from one private product, without exposing its code or data.</p></div>
      <div class="project-grid">{systems.map((project) => <a class={`project-card accent-${project.accent}`} href={`/en/projects/${project.slug}/`}><div class="project-top"><span>{project.number} / SYSTEM</span><span class="card-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div><div class="project-art" aria-hidden="true"><span class="art-frame"><span class="art-grid"></span><span class="art-symbol">{project.number === '02' ? '↔' : project.number === '03' ? '◫' : project.number === '04' ? '▣' : '◇'}</span></span></div><div class="project-copy"><p class="project-type">{project.type}</p><h3>{project.title}</h3><p>{project.description}</p><div class="tags">{project.stack.map((skill) => <span>{skill}</span>)}</div></div></a>)}</div>
    </section>
    <section class="section skills-section" id="tecnologias"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="section-kicker">02 / EXPERTISE</p><h2>Tools for<br /><em>each layer.</em></h2></div><p>Each listed technology has an identifiable role in a reviewed project.</p></div><div class="capability-grid"><div class="capability-card"><div class="capability-number">01</div><h3>Product and interfaces</h3><p>Multiplatform apps, interactive scenes and web products.</p><div class="skill-list">{['Dart','Flutter','Flame','JavaScript','TypeScript','Astro','Next.js','React'].map((skill) => <span>{skill}</span>)}</div></div><div class="capability-card"><div class="capability-number">02</div><h3>Systems and integration</h3><p>Native logic, local synchronization, persistence and Android integration.</p><div class="skill-list">{['Rust','Kotlin','Flutter Rust Bridge','Isar','Supabase/Postgres','LAN/P2P'].map((skill) => <span>{skill}</span>)}</div></div></div><p class="skills-note">C, C++, Assembly, Swift and PHP/Laravel are listed in the lab as planned samples until independent code is ready for review.</p></div></section>
    <section class="section wrap architecture-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="section-kicker">03 / ARCHITECTURE</p><h2>Built for unstable<br /><em>connections.</em></h2></div><p>Local operations do not depend on cloud availability for every action.</p></div><div class="architecture-grid"><div class="architecture-diagram" aria-label="Point of sale, floor and kitchen devices communicate locally, then synchronize remotely"><div class="diagram-label">MESON / LOCAL NETWORK</div><div class="diagram-devices"><span>POS</span><span>FLOOR</span><span>KITCHEN</span></div><div class="diagram-flow">↔ &nbsp; DISCOVERY + P2P MESSAGES &nbsp; ↔</div><div class="diagram-store">LOCAL DATA AND QUEUE</div><div class="diagram-arrow">↓ when connected</div><div class="diagram-cloud">REMOTE SYNC</div></div><div class="architecture-copy"><div><span>01</span><h3>Local work</h3><p>Devices can exchange changes over the restaurant network during an Internet outage.</p></div><div><span>02</span><h3>Native network layer</h3><p>The Rust engine implements encrypted envelopes and replay controls.</p></div><div><span>03</span><h3>Connection recovery</h3><p>Local persistence and a queue keep pending changes until remote services return.</p></div><a class="text-link" href="/en/projects/red-p2p/">Explore the architecture ↗</a></div></div><p class="architecture-caveat">During a power outage, devices need batteries and the local network needs backup power.</p></section>
    <section class="section wrap about-section" id="sobre-mi"><div><p class="section-kicker">04 / APPROACH</p><h2>Broad view.<br /><em>Clear outcomes.</em></h2></div><div class="about-copy"><p>I am interested in software that works in its real operating context. That means working on the user journey as well as data, performance, integration and maintainability.</p><p>I have led most of Meson's design and implementation, with selected Flutter contributions from another developer. The full codebase remains private; these cases explain the product without releasing sensitive code or data.</p><a class="text-link" href="/en/projects/meson/">Read the Meson case ↗</a></div></section>
    <section class="contact-section"><div class="wrap contact-inner"><p class="section-kicker">05 / CONTACT</p><h2>Let's build<br /><em>useful software.</em></h2><p>Open to discussing software engineering opportunities.</p><div class="contact-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href={profile.github} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub ↗</a>{profile.linkedin && <a class="button button-outline" href={profile.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn ↗</a>}{profile.email && <a class="button button-outline" href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}>Email ↗</a>}</div></div></section>
  </main>
</Base>
